          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:262d32b0792de71b3912578c8d932cf45df8cd83f5d98355d327d094a57aec40:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_40447e1957a14969ab82081c8b593e17",
      "statement": "POST /wikis layers git protocol policy on top of validate_git_url and rejects with HTTP 422 before creating a job: a source.auth.token is only accepted for http:// or https:// URLs; push is refused for git@/ssh:// sources because SSH keys are not available in the service; push is refused for git:// URLs; and an http(s) push without a token is refused because it would be anonymous.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/routers/wikis.py#L50-L89",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:162e5521a337df5b0e4d39996afb39e20a862fbc1db45e284811ad7bb2b1bb50:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6e5b07bb4b7e4f55ac18774c6df83d88",
      "statement": "run_git_status(args, cwd, secrets, timeout_seconds) runs git and returns a redacted (exit_code, stdout, stderr) tuple without raising on non-zero exit, killing the process and raising IngestionError on timeout; run_git() wraps it, returning stdout and raising IngestionError with the last eight lines of stderr (or stdout) when the exit code is non-zero. The status variant exists because several git commands use the exit code as data (git diff --cached --quiet, rev-parse, symbolic-ref, check-ref-format, ls-remote), which an always-raising wrapper would make unusable.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/services/ingestion.py#L112-L164",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f416587e57c439bbadd548f153edebe649c3582cdc63c2d6db28990168a9feb2:"
