    {
      "id": "claim_50d2fa1da9ea4c17b90dad27f57f5ad0",
      "statement": "ensure_git_repo(repo_dir) makes git available for sources that lack it: it returns False when .git already exists, otherwise runs git init --quiet, git add --all and git commit --quiet --allow-empty -m 'Import source for OpenWiki'. The identity (user.email=openwiki-service@localhost, user.name=openwiki-service) is passed per command with -c rather than configured globally, so the image needs no git identity in the environment; --allow-empty keeps an empty archive valid. The pipeline calls it after every fetch, so it is a no-op for git sources and the effective path only for uploads without .git.",
