    {
      "id": "claim_69d98cff589f465c94e6680baac277c2",
      "statement": "The container image configures safe.directory system-wide because git refuses to operate on repositories owned by another user (dubious ownership) and safe.directory is only honoured from system or global configuration, never from git -c: the Dockerfile adds git config --system --add safe.directory '*' before switching to appuser (uid 10001), trusting every directory inside the container. Outside Docker this configuration is absent, so an operator hitting a dubious-ownership error must run git config --global --add safe.directory <path> themselves.",
      "evidence": [
